    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Hello, Kelly. It's your coeliac follow-up. You've been on the gluten-free diet for six months now. How's it going?",
      "start_timestamp": "00:53",
      "end_timestamp": "01:02",
      "supports": [
        "chief_complaint"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_003",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "And the bloating, and the loose stools you had before?",
      "start_timestamp": "01:19",
      "end_timestamp": "01:25",
      "supports": [
        "negative_findings[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "Gone. Well, almost. I haven't had a bad day in two months. No diarrhoea at all.",
      "start_timestamp": "01:27",
      "end_timestamp": "01:37",
      "supports": [
        "negative_findings[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Are you taking anything at the moment?",
      "start_timestamp": "01:54",
      "end_timestamp": "01:58",
      "supports": [
        "medications[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "A vitamin D tablet, 1000 units, once a day. And an iron tablet last year, but I've stopped.",
      "start_timestamp": "01:58",
      "end_timestamp": "02:08",
      "supports": [
        "medications[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Any other conditions?",
      "start_timestamp": "02:09",
      "end_timestamp": "02:11",
      "supports": [
        "medical_history.past_medical_history[0]",
        "medical_history.past_medical_history[1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "An underactive thyroid, and a bit of eczema.",
      "start_timestamp": "02:13",
      "end_timestamp": "02:18",
      "supports": [
        "medical_history.past_medical_history[0]",
        "medical_history.past_medical_history[1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Do you drink alcohol?",
      "start_timestamp": "02:20",
      "end_timestamp": "02:23",
      "supports": [
        "medical_history.social_history[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "speaker_role": "patient",
      "transcript_text": "Cider, or wine, at weekends. And gluten-free beer, I've discovered.",
      "start_timestamp": "02:26",
      "end_timestamp": "02:31",
      "supports": [
        "medical_history.social_history[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Your tummy is soft, no tenderness, and no bloating, and your skin looks healthy, no rash.",
      "start_timestamp": "03:00",
      "end_timestamp": "03:09",
      "supports": [
        "physical_examination[0]",
        "physical_examination[1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Yes, it's responding very well to the diet. I'd say your coeliac disease is well controlled on the gluten-free diet.",
      "start_timestamp": "03:42",
      "end_timestamp": "03:52",
      "supports": [
        "clinical_assessment[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "I'd like to repeat the blood test in six months, to make sure the antibody stays down, and I'd like to arrange a bone density check, because coeliac can affect bones.",
      "start_timestamp": "04:00",
      "end_timestamp": "04:16",
      "supports": [
        "procedures_and_investigations[0]",
        "procedures_and_investigations[1]",
        "clinical_actions[0]",
        "clinical_actions[1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Keep the diet strictly, even small amounts of gluten can keep the damage going. And watch cross-contamination, toasters and spreads.",
      "start_timestamp": "04:19",
      "end_timestamp": "04:30",
      "supports": [
        "clinical_actions[3]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "That's the way. I'd also like you to see the dietitian once a year, and have the flu jab.",
      "start_timestamp": "04:37",
      "end_timestamp": "04:49",
      "supports": [
        "clinical_actions[4]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "If your symptoms come back, or you lose weight, get a rash with blisters, or become very tired, come back sooner.",
      "start_timestamp": "05:07",
      "end_timestamp": "05:18",
